::ENG3_U02_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.R.02] Passage: The village bridge had fallen in the flood. An old carpenter set one plank across the gap and waited. By evening, a child brought a second plank, and by morning, every family had added one board. Which universal theme is best supported? {
=Shared responsibility can turn one person's first action into a community effort.#Correct. The theme is stated as a complete idea and is supported by the villagers adding boards.
~Bridges are always stronger than floods.#This is too literal and not fully supported.
~Children should build bridges without adults.#This is not the message of the passage.
~Floods always help villages improve.#This overgeneralizes and misreads the damage.
}

::ENG3_U02_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.R.02] Text A: A traveler shares his last water with a stranger and later survives because the stranger knows the way to the city. Text B: A student shares study notes and later receives help preparing for a speech. What universal theme do both texts develop? {
~Technology changes how people learn.#Neither text focuses on technology.
=Generosity can create unexpected support.#Correct. Both texts show one act of giving leading to help later.
~Travel is more dangerous than school.#This compares settings but misses the shared theme.
~People should never accept help.#Both texts show help as valuable.
}

::ENG3_U02_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.R.02] Text A develops generosity through a desert survival situation. Text B develops generosity through a school situation. What does this show about universal themes? {
~Universal themes only appear in old stories.#Text B shows a modern setting.
~Universal themes require identical plots.#The plots differ, but the theme is shared.
=Universal themes can appear in different settings and still explore similar human concerns.#Correct. The same theme can develop across different times and places.
~Universal themes cannot include evidence.#Theme analysis requires evidence.
}

::ENG3_U02_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.02] Text A: A sailor teaches children to read stars after ships begin using machines. Text B: A coding mentor teaches students to sketch ideas before opening laptops. Which shared theme is best? {
~Machines are always bad.#Both texts include technology but do not reject it completely.
~Older people are always wiser than younger people.#The texts focus on foundational skills, not age superiority.
~Travel and coding are the same activity.#This is a surface comparison, not a theme.
=Basic skills remain valuable even when tools change.#Correct. Both texts show older or non-digital skills still mattering.
}

::ENG3_U02_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.R.02] Which statement is the best theme statement? {
~Courage#This is a topic, not a complete theme.
=Courage often begins with a small action taken despite fear.#Correct. This is a complete insight about courage.
~A brave character in a dangerous place#This is a plot description, not a theme.
~The text is about courage.#This identifies a topic but does not state what the text says about it.
}
